Usage: agent-deck deepseek <command> [--json]

Inspect the DeepSeek Harness (`dsh`) integration: which binary agent-deck
would launch, which DSH_HOME it resolves, which profiles exist there, and
which conversations a workspace has. Read-only.

Commands:
  status                  Resolved binary, version, DSH_HOME, profile, resume support
  profiles                List the profiles under $DSH_HOME/profiles
  sessions [workspace]    List dsh session IDs recorded for a workspace
                          (defaults to the current directory)
  help                    Show this help message

Flags:
  --json                  Emit machine-readable JSON instead of text

Configuration lives in [deepseek] (command, config_dir, profile, patches,
host, port, trusted_hosts, resume_flag, extra_args, env_file), with
per-account overrides in [profiles.<account>.deepseek].config_dir.

Launch a session with:  agent-deck launch -c deepseek
Install the CLI with:   npm install -g @deepseek-ai/dsh
